[[:db/retract 17592186106512 :question/answer-fields 17592186105220] {:db/id 17592186105827 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8dd54609-ae0c-53a9-a2a1-7823f9aa6595" "question-46c22425-ee4e-5a56-9d8f-8f1ffa9ada86" "question-29a87319-221e-52be-a49a-7a7f42765bfa" "question-e06f09da-f1cd-5f64-925a-f4c6e513e373"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105825 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8e0e75d6-02e9-556c-b809-4824d53487ed" "question-48a19d94-de64-5ea0-b742-40601b9c76a4" "question-c93c3864-ab3f-5794-a142-3eab6e62d56b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105826 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-265e293f-7554-5958-abfd-df783c671c82" "question-ec42c1b6-69ea-5d9d-b8b5-5ad8c82e5789" "question-f0df1382-8e7a-5174-b609-3e041c2744d5" "question-90500394-6fc0-5ba4-a5dc-ea52dd5425de" "question-69ccd3d4-6bc6-5b97-931d-42636fcb0b40"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105830 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7a3cf3a8-b182-51ac-8e52-79ae8f41f3ac" "question-cfd01f57-c0cd-576d-bb6c-c4a4c9533c2d" "question-6d707ab1-b369-599a-9705-58f642e1bb10" "question-b1efc3f5-91c0-5d80-b7bf-74abaff81c0a" "question-a48cf853-bbc5-5226-99de-0617e7d6b622"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8dd54609-ae0c-53a9-a2a1-7823f9aa6595" :question/id #uuid "8dd54609-ae0c-53a9-a2a1-7823f9aa6595" :question/math-academy-id "q-84747" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables could be modeled as a binomial distribution?\n\n- The number of times \"head\" is obtained when a coin is tossed $10$ times\n- The number of students in a class\n- The number of tickets sold for a concert in $3$ days" :question/worked-solution "A binomial distribution models the number of successes in a sequence of $n$ independent experiments (where each outcome is either success or failure).\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable I could be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of \"heads\" in $10$ tosses can be interpreted as the number of successes in a sequence of $10$ independent experiments.\n\n- Random variable II could *not* be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of students in a class cannot be interpreted as \"success\" or \"failure.\"\n\n- Random variable III could *not* be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of tickets sold for a concert cannot be interpreted as \"success\" or \"failure.\"\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0b85b9db-4b3a-5931-a044-422d92ddf7c1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0b85b9db-4b3a-5931-a044-422d92ddf7c1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0b85b9db-4b3a-5931-a044-422d92ddf7c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-21ae41fa-236b-530c-90e6-fb5cf9abc0e0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4a98ac69-4946-50af-be1a-a87eda63d1a6" "answer-21ae41fa-236b-530c-90e6-fb5cf9abc0e0" "answer-dd3a5183-df01-521a-be7e-92566b8b266a" "answer-51ae6abc-b491-5c69-9fda-9c44145f964f" "answer-de49179b-7a0c-5bcd-ab74-23a6fdd2bd82"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a98ac69-4946-50af-be1a-a87eda63d1a6" :answer/id #uuid "4a98ac69-4946-50af-be1a-a87eda63d1a6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21ae41fa-236b-530c-90e6-fb5cf9abc0e0" :answer/id #uuid "21ae41fa-236b-530c-90e6-fb5cf9abc0e0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd3a5183-df01-521a-be7e-92566b8b266a" :answer/id #uuid "dd3a5183-df01-521a-be7e-92566b8b266a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-51ae6abc-b491-5c69-9fda-9c44145f964f" :answer/id #uuid "51ae6abc-b491-5c69-9fda-9c44145f964f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de49179b-7a0c-5bcd-ab74-23a6fdd2bd82" :answer/id #uuid "de49179b-7a0c-5bcd-ab74-23a6fdd2bd82" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-46c22425-ee4e-5a56-9d8f-8f1ffa9ada86" :question/id #uuid "46c22425-ee4e-5a56-9d8f-8f1ffa9ada86" :question/math-academy-id "q-84748" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables could be modeled as a binomial distribution?\n\n- The ages of $20$ soccer players\n- The price of a pair of pants in a department store\n- The number of wins by a basketball team in a $30$-game season if the probability of the team winning any individual game is $55%$" :question/worked-solution "A binomial distribution models the number of successes in a sequence of $n$ independent experiments (where each outcome is either success or failure).\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable I could *not* be modeled as a binomial distribution. The ages cannot be interpreted as \"success\" or \"failure.\"\n\n- Random variable II could *not* be modeled as a binomial distribution. The prices cannot be interpreted as \"success\" or \"failure.\"\n\n- Random variable III could be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of wins in $30$ games can be interpreted as the number of successes in a sequence of $30$ independent experiments.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d22af52a-6cb4-5c75-ae52-e745c13307b9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d22af52a-6cb4-5c75-ae52-e745c13307b9" :answer-field/id #uuid "d22af52a-6cb4-5c75-ae52-e745c13307b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f93fce79-3e49-557b-96a5-c10f504fd798" :answer-field/choices ["answer-41c0fe61-4cd5-5060-819b-ff762f83aae0" "answer-5481292b-246a-5d52-93ec-b37d3c